    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0115" n="50" xml:id="pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3963: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-20T18:00:00+02:35">March 20, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>170. Have just received <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> from Ethiopian
                    Foreign Office dated today protesting formally against constant violation by
                    Italy of article XXIII (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) and article XXV of Hague
                    Convention No. 4 of 1907<anchor n="20" xml:id="d51-f1"/> and Geneva Protocol of
                    June 17, 1925,<anchor n="21" xml:id="d51-f2"/> by using asphyxiating gases and
                    bombing civilian populations.</p>
                <p>Ethiopian Government reserves all rights under article III of said Hague
                    Convention and appeals to the Government of the United States as one of the
                    signatories of the above-mentioned convention and protocol “to be good enough to
                    take all measure it may deem proper to cause the enemy to desist immediately
                    from the said violations.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
